  "notes": "Three-page charity financial statements (one statement per page; the notes start on page 3). The letter-spaced organisation line at the top of page 1 is letterhead furniture; the bottom-left footer is listed once and the bare page number once per page. Tables are PARTLY RULED (rules only under headers, above subtotals, double rule under totals). Section rows ('Non-current assets', 'Income', 'Cost or valuation' ...) carry their label in the first cell only; the other cells are empty strings. Subtotal rows have an empty label cell. Negative amounts are in parentheses. The statement of activities has a TWO-LEVEL header (first cell and '2025 Total' span two rows; '2026' spans three columns). Note headings ('1 Accounting policies' ...) are level 3. The two signature blocks sit side by side."
